            <ArticleTitle>[Changes in the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system in the development of hypertension in aging. 2].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The change of the reactivity of the RAAS during physiological aging of the organism implies the variety of forms of the course of hypertension: The RAAS is involved in stage I of the development of the disease. The progress of the disease (stage III) results in the &quot;decay&quot; of the RAAS. A dependence of the activity of the RAAS on the clinical course and on the hemodynamic variant of hypertension in old age could detected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
